---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import AdvertiserDisclosure from '../../components/AdvertiserDisclosure.astro';
import AmazonButton from '../../components/AmazonButton.astro';
import PlannerCTA from '../../components/PlannerCTA.astro';

const reviewedAt = 'August 15, 2026';

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'Do I need a sauna labeled for one person?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'No. Many compact cabins are labeled for one to two people, and small traditional rooms are often labeled for two. A solo buyer should compare the exact interior dimensions, bench length, heat format, electrical requirements, and complete project cost instead of shopping by capacity alone.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'Can a solo sauna use a 120V outlet?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'Some compact infrared cabins and portable steam enclosures list 120V service. Traditional electric sauna heaters commonly require a dedicated hardwired circuit. Use the current manual for the exact model and have site electrical conditions checked when the instructions require it.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'What should I measure for an indoor solo sauna?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'Measure the final floor area, ceiling height, doorway, stairs, turning space, assembly clearance, door swing, outlet location, and required clearances. Compare those measurements with the current product manual before ordering.',
      },
    },
  ],
};
---
<Base
  title="Solo Home Saunas: Three Current Formats"
  description="Compare an indoor infrared cabin, portable steam enclosure, and compact traditional barrel for solo use using current specs and complete-project checks."
  canonical="/guides/best-1-person-sauna"
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />

  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
    <header class="max-w-3xl mb-8">
      <p class="text-sm text-amber-700 font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide mb-2">Solo sauna buying guide</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-stone-900 leading-tight mb-4">Solo Home Saunas: Three Current Formats</h1>
      <p class="text-stone-500 text-sm">Product routes reviewed {reviewedAt} - 9 min read</p>
      <p class="text-lg text-stone-700 mt-4">A solo buyer does not need the smallest product on the page. You need the smallest complete setup that fits your room, preferred heat, power, cleaning routine, and budget.</p>
    </header>

    <AdvertiserDisclosure />

    <figure class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden mb-8">
      <img src="/images/lifestyle/sauna-interior-forest-view.jpg" alt="Compact wood sauna interior with a window" class="w-full object-cover max-h-80" loading="eager" width="1200" height="800" />
      <figcaption class="text-xs text-stone-500 mt-2">Representative sauna interior. It is not a photo of the exact products discussed below.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <aside class="border-y border-stone-200 py-6 mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-2">Choose the format before the product</h2>
      <p class="text-stone-700 mb-3">An infrared cabin, steam tent, and traditional barrel differ in heat source, installation, moisture, maintenance, portability, and total cost. Treating them as interchangeable “one-person saunas” hides the decision that matters most.</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-stone-600">We did not hands-on test these products. We reviewed manufacturer specifications and the exact commerce routes listed here. Stock, seller, price, delivery, and warranty terms can change.</p>
    </aside>

    <PlannerCTA
      source="solo_sauna_above_fold"
      heading="Match the format to your room and utilities"
      description="Build a private brief with the installation location, available space, power, delivery path, heat preference, and complete budget before choosing a compact unit."
    />

    <section class="mt-12" aria-labelledby="solo-formats">
      <h2 id="solo-formats" class="text-3xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3">Three current solo-use formats</h2>
      <p class="text-stone-600 max-w-3xl mb-8">These are representative current products, not a universal ranking. Each one earns a place only when its format fits the buyer's actual constraints.</p>

      <section class="border-t border-stone-300 pt-7" aria-labelledby="solo-infrared">
        <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-amber-700 mb-2">Permanent indoor cabin</p>
        <h3 id="solo-infrared" class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3">Dynamic Saunas Barcelona DYN-6106-01</h3>
        <p class="text-stone-700 mb-5">A compact infrared cabin for a buyer with dedicated indoor floor space. Dynamic labels it for one to two people. Used solo, its published 36-inch interior width leaves more room than a two-person session would.</p>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-7">
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3">Documented details</h4>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-stone-700 list-disc pl-5">
              <li>Published exterior size: 39 by 36 by 73 inches</li>
              <li>Published interior size: 36 by 32 by 67 inches</li>
              <li>Published electrical service: 120V, 15A</li>
              <li>Hemlock cabin, six carbon heating panels, tempered glass, and controls</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3">Verify before checkout</h4>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-stone-700 list-disc pl-5">
              <li>Doorway, stairs, ceiling, floor, assembly clearance, and door swing</li>
              <li>Current seller, stock, delivered price, returns, and warranty</li>
              <li>Outlet location and the manual's circuit and cord instructions</li>
              <li>Any EMF claim's method, distance, and numerical test result</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
          <AmazonButton asin="B00A2F99F0" label="Check the current Barcelona listing" variant="primary" ctaPosition="solo_infrared" />
          <a href="https://dynamicsaunasdirect.com/products/barcelona-1-2-person-low-emf-far-infrared-sauna" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-sm font-semibold text-amber-700 hover:underline">Review manufacturer specifications</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="border-t border-stone-300 pt-7 mt-10" aria-labelledby="solo-steam">
        <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-amber-700 mb-2">Portable steam enclosure</p>
        <h3 id="solo-steam" class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3">SereneLife SLISAU35BK</h3>
        <p class="text-stone-700 mb-5">A foldable steam enclosure for a buyer who prioritizes storage and a smaller initial commitment. It is not an infrared cabin or a traditional room with heated stones.</p>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-7">
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3">Documented details</h4>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-stone-700 list-disc pl-5">
              <li>Published enclosure size: 35.43 by 35.43 by 70.87 inches</li>
              <li>Published 1600-watt steamer and 120V power</li>
              <li>Nine heat settings, remote control, and folding chair are listed</li>
              <li>Low-water shutoff and a model-specific manual are available</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3">Verify before checkout</h4>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-stone-700 list-disc pl-5">
              <li>Floor protection plus room to drain, wipe, dry, and store it</li>
              <li>Current seller, included parts, warranty, and return process</li>
              <li>Outlet location and the manual's electrical instructions</li>
              <li>Replacement availability for the steamer, hose, liner, and chair</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
          <AmazonButton asin="B084GY5CHB" label="Check the current SereneLife listing" variant="primary" ctaPosition="solo_steam" />
          <a href="https://serenelifehome.com/collections/new-arrivals/products/slisau35bk" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-sm font-semibold text-amber-700 hover:underline">Review manufacturer specifications</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="border-t border-stone-300 pt-7 mt-10" aria-labelledby="solo-traditional">
        <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-amber-700 mb-2">Traditional outdoor room</p>
        <h3 id="solo-traditional" class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3">Almost Heaven Salem 2-Person Barrel</h3>
        <p class="text-stone-700 mb-5">A compact traditional sauna for a homeowner who accepts an outdoor base, freight delivery, assembly, and hardwired heater. Its two published 39-inch benches do not provide a full reclining bench, even for one user.</p>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-7">
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3">Documented details</h4>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-stone-700 list-disc pl-5">
              <li>Published assembled size: 72 by 47 by 77 inches</li>
              <li>Published interior size: 71 by 39 by 71 inches</li>
              <li>Two 39-inch-long benches and a 540-pound shipping weight</li>
              <li>Standard 6kW heater listed for 240V, 30A hardwired service</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3">Verify before checkout</h4>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-stone-700 list-disc pl-5">
              <li>Exact wood, door, window, heater, controls, stones, and warranty</li>
              <li>Freight, unloading, assembly access, and lead time</li>
              <li>Level base, drainage, weather exposure, and anchoring</li>
              <li>Current manual, permits, disconnect, and licensed electrical scope</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
          <a
            href="https://selectsaunas.com/products/almost-heaven-salem-2-person-barrel-sauna?sca_ref=10752576.S2huPg7gFg"
            target="_blank"
            rel="nofollow noopener sponsored"
            class="inline-block bg-amber-500 hover:bg-amber-600 text-white font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded-lg transition-colors text-sm"
            data-cta-position="solo_traditional"
            data-product-id="almost-heaven-salem-2-person"
            data-link-mode="verified_product"
            data-partner="select_saunas"
          >Check the current Salem configuration</a>
          <a href="https://almostheaven.com/products/salem-2-person-barrel-sauna" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-sm font-semibold text-amber-700 hover:underline">Review manufacturer specifications</a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12 border-t border-stone-300 pt-8" aria-labelledby="solo-comparison">
      <h2 id="solo-comparison" class="text-3xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-6">Match the format to the constraint</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full min-w-[720px] text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-b border-stone-300 text-left text-stone-600">
              <th class="pb-3 pr-5">Priority</th>
              <th class="pb-3 pr-5">Infrared cabin</th>
              <th class="pb-3 pr-5">Steam enclosure</th>
              <th class="pb-3">Traditional barrel</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="text-stone-700">
            <tr class="border-b border-stone-200"><td class="py-3 pr-5 font-semibold">Dedicated space</td><td class="py-3 pr-5">Permanent indoor footprint</td><td class="py-3 pr-5">Can be drained and stored</td><td class="py-3">Permanent outdoor project</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-stone-200"><td class="py-3 pr-5 font-semibold">Heat format</td><td class="py-3 pr-5">Infrared panels</td><td class="py-3 pr-5">Steam generator</td><td class="py-3">Electric heater and stones</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-stone-200"><td class="py-3 pr-5 font-semibold">Published power</td><td class="py-3 pr-5">120V, 15A</td><td class="py-3 pr-5">120V, 1600W</td><td class="py-3">240V, 30A hardwired heater</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="py-3 pr-5 font-semibold">Main burden</td><td class="py-3 pr-5">Indoor access and assembly</td><td class="py-3 pr-5">Cleaning, drying, and storage</td><td class="py-3">Base, delivery, assembly, and electrical work</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12 border-t border-stone-300 pt-8" aria-labelledby="solo-budget">
      <h2 id="solo-budget" class="text-3xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3">Price the complete setup</h2>
      <p class="text-stone-700 mb-5">Include delivery, access, floor or base work, electrical work, assembly, cleaning supplies, permits, tax, and likely replacement parts. Comparing three sticker prices would misrepresent three very different projects.</p>
      <a href="/tools/sauna-cost-calculator/?utm_source=solo_sauna&utm_medium=onsite&utm_campaign=project_budget" class="inline-block bg-stone-900 hover:bg-stone-800 text-white font-semibold px-5 py-3 rounded-md" data-cta-position="solo_project_budget">Build the full project budget</a>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12 border-t border-stone-300 pt-8" aria-labelledby="solo-faq">
      <h2 id="solo-faq" class="text-3xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-6">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="divide-y divide-stone-200 border-y border-stone-200">
        <div class="py-5"><h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-2">Do I need a sauna labeled for one person?</h3><p class="text-stone-700">No. Compare measured fit, heat format, utilities, and total cost. A compact one-to-two-person product may be the practical solo choice.</p></div>
        <div class="py-5"><h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-2">Can a solo sauna use a 120V outlet?</h3><p class="text-stone-700">Some infrared cabins and steam enclosures do. Traditional electric heaters commonly require a dedicated hardwired circuit. Follow the exact product manual.</p></div>
        <div class="py-5"><h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-2">What should I measure indoors?</h3><p class="text-stone-700">Measure floor area, ceiling height, doorway, stairs, turning space, assembly clearance, door swing, outlet location, and required clearances.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <aside class="mt-12 border border-stone-200 rounded-lg p-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3">Continue comparing</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
        <li><a href="/guides/best-2-person-sauna/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Two-person sauna fit guide</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/best-portable-sauna/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Portable sauna format guide</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/best-sauna-for-small-backyard/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Small-backyard sauna guide</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/sauna-electrical-requirements/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Sauna electrical planning</a></li>
      </ul>
    </aside>
  </article>
</Base>
